service.go:14: input Config/Options struct Config declares exported Clock field of type clock.Clock; clock must enter via positional parameter, not struct literal — struct-field injection lets callers omit the clock at compile time. ref: docs/architecture/202605270000-adr-clock-positional-injection-funnel.md
service.go:25: clock.MustHaveClock: arg0 must be a function parameter (positional injection); selector or non-ident arg0 (e.g. cfg.Clock, s.clk) violates the positional-param contract. ref: docs/architecture/202605270000-adr-clock-positional-injection-funnel.md
